; walk-cxx-past-end — a break past the target pattern's last row.
;
; `C05` on pattern 0's row 0 breaks to row 5 of the next order, whose
; pattern has two rows. The ruling (plan 09): it lands on ROW 0 OF THAT
; PATTERN, which is what IT itself and OpenMPT do — it does not step on
; to the order after it. Under the old rule this walk played one row and
; stopped; under this one it plays three.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
